\"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:22\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073913c48a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1c03168edc496741\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26301305364159244, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05837146234513209, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7405101, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073913c48a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:22\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Group: Review and approve the PR.\\n\\n### 4) PR: Counter performance improvements; benchmarks and exemplar behavior\\n\\n- Summary:\\n\\n  - Significant optimization work on synchronous metric paths:\\n\\n    - Use sync.Map for attribute-set storage to improve read-heavy performance.\\n\\n    - Atomic sum values; “hot-cold” waitgroup technique to make measurements lockless and enable safe resets for delta aggregations (inspired by Prometheus histogram patterns).\\n\\n  - Known implications:\\n\\n    - Attribute-set limit becomes a soft limit due to race in attribute-set creation (map size tracking vs. map updates).\\n\\n    - For cumulative aggregations, enforcing attribute limits deterministically is harder since state persists; care needed to avoid inconsistent drops.\\n\\n    - Exemplar behavior: an Add may be included in the metric points but its exemplar may not be recorded in the same batch, which is acceptable and consistent with Prometheus and exemplar sampling design.\\n\\n- Discussion highlights:\\n\\n  - Potential follow-up: for exemplar reservoirs, a “merge” API could enable hot-cold reservoir consolidation for stricter atomicity at a higher level.\\n\\n  - Future performance work: histogram improvements and sharding (e.g., per-CPU) to reduce contention further.\\n\\n  - Benchmarks indicate substantial gains: ~10x for histograms with no contention; ~3x for fixed-size with shared contention.\\n\\n- Decisions:\\n\\n  - Accept current approach; exemplar variability is acceptable under spec/practice.\\n\\n  - Prioritize reviews for the benchmark PR and counter performance PR; histograms/fixed-size follow after.\\n\\n- Action items:\\n\\n  - David:\\n\\n    - Finalize and sequence PRs: benchmark fix (includes bug fix), counter performance improvements, then histogram/fixed-size improvements.\\n\\n    - Document soft-limit behavior and any mitigation for cumulative aggregations.\\n\\n  - Tyler/Group: Review benchmark PR and counter performance PR first; provide feedback and approvals.\\n\\n  - Tyler: Consider options to tie map-size accounting to updates more atomically; follow up with comments/ideas.\\n\\n## Decisions (summary)\\n\\n- Ownership and ops first: Establish clear owner, access, notifications, and playbooks for go.opentelemetry.io; explore migration to Netlify/Hugo only with owners’ approval.\\n\\n- Scope naming: Use instrumentation library name per spec; later add an attribute for the instrumented component/package (track via semantic conventions).\\n\\n- Error types: Adopt domain-specific error.type where available; proceed after GoDoc verification.\\n\\n- Performance work: Accept exemplar sampling variability; proceed with benchmark and counter performance PRs; histograms/fixed-size next.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"group review and approv the pr 4 pr counter perform improv benchmark and exemplar behavior summari signific optim work on synchron metric path use sync map for attribut set storag to improv read heavi perform atom sum valu hot cold waitgroup techniqu to make measur lockless and enabl safe reset for delta aggreg inspir by prometheus histogram pattern known implic attribut set limit becom a soft limit due to race in attribut set creation map size track v map updat for cumul aggreg enforc attribut limit determinist is harder sinc state persist care need to avoid inconsist drop exemplar behavior an add may be includ in the metric point but it exemplar may not be record in the same batch which is accept and consist with prometheus and exemplar sampl design discuss highlight potenti follow up for exemplar reservoir a merg api could enabl hot cold reservoir consolid for stricter atom at a higher level futur perform work histogram improv and shard e g per cpu to reduc content further benchmark indic substanti gain 10x for histogram with no content 3x for fix size with share content decis accept current approach exemplar variabl is accept under spec practic priorit review for the benchmark pr and counter perform pr histogram fix size follow after action item david final and sequenc pr benchmark fix includ bug fix counter perform improv then histogram fix size improv document soft limit behavior and ani mitig for cumul aggreg tyler group review benchmark pr and counter perform pr first provid feedback and approv tyler consid option to tie map size account to updat more atom follow up with comment idea decis summari ownership and op first establish clear owner access notif and playbook for go opentelemetri io explor migrat to netlifi hugo onli with owner approv scope name use instrument librari name per spec later add an attribut for the instrument compon packag track via semant convent error type adopt domain specif error type where avail proceed after godoc verif perform work accept exemplar sampl variabl proceed with benchmark and counter perform pr histogram fix size next\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073b2c548a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"id\": \"7eb387600d062c48\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26053358823794504, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07004575462563575, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7050052, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073b2c548a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8301, \"chunk_count\": 7, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:23\", \"token_count\": 3187, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Seek more engagement from gRPC; attempt in-person conversations at KubeCon if possible. David will sync with Josh on outreach.\\n\\n- Conclusion: Not likely to stabilize this year; set a goal to finalize a strategy next year once semconv progress is clearer.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Stabilization of otelgrpc](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078)?\\n\\n  - Related: [https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265)  \\n\\n  - We need the semconv to stabilize  \\n\\n  - There needs to be involvement from gRPC to progress this  \\n\\n  - [David] Update: I’m told that the SIG is active and is working towards stabilization. Not sure if gRPC is involved.  \\n\\n### Stabilization of otelhttp\\n\\n- Damien proposed starting an API audit for otelhttp to move towards stabilization.\\n\\n- A known bug (issue #7254) may be the only blocker; it’s a behavioral change around how errors are marked (events vs attributes) and interacts with semconv/spec wording.\\n\\n- Agreement:\\n\\n  - Begin the API review.\\n\\n  - Robert will take ownership of #7254 and draft a document clarifying interpretation and proposed resolution.\\n\\n  - The existence of bugs does not inherently block stabilization; they can be fixed post-stabilization if changes are non-breaking or properly versioned.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- Blocker (only one I think): [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254)  \\n\\n### OTel Explorer Go docs\\n\\n- Mike outlined a project to revamp the OTEL registry/explorer with a schema that documents spans/metrics emitted by instrumentations, aiming to render via Hugo and enable static analysis across Go SDKs and contrib modules.\\n\\n- Tyler’s feedback:\\n\\n  - Strong requirement: align schema with semantic conventions and ensure it’s compatible with Weaver (to enable validation and transformations across versions).\\n\\n  - Consider providing a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation and potentially linking to existing semconv definitions to keep the spec concise.\\n\\n  - Scope can include eBPF/auto-instrumentation; representation should still fit the schema as long as it maps to OTEL signals.\\n\\n- Mike will iterate on the schema, explore Weaver integration, and coordinate with SIGs as needed.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n  - Context: [https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000)  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"seek more engag from grpc attempt in person convers at kubecon if possibl david will sync with josh on outreach conclus not like to stabil this year set a goal to final a strategi next year onc semconv progress is clearer refer stabil of otelgrpc http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 relat http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 we need the semconv to stabil there need to be involv from grpc to progress this david updat i m told that the sig is activ and is work toward stabil not sure if grpc is involv stabil of otelhttp damien propos start an api audit for otelhttp to move toward stabil a known bug issu 7254 may be the onli blocker it s a behavior chang around how error are mark event v attribut and interact with semconv spec word agreement begin the api review robert will take ownership of 7254 and draft a document clarifi interpret and propos resolut the exist of bug doe not inher block stabil they can be fix post stabil if chang are non break or proper version refer blocker onli one i think http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 otel explor go doc mike outlin a project to revamp the otel registri explor with a schema that document span metric emit by instrument aim to render via hugo and enabl static analysi across go sdks and contrib modul tyler s feedback strong requir align schema with semant convent and ensur it s compat with weaver to enabl valid and transform across version consid provid a json schema or cue for valid and potenti link to exist semconv definit to keep the spec concis scope can includ ebpf auto instrument represent should still fit the schema a long a it map to otel signal mike will iter on the schema explor weaver integr and coordin with sig a need refer context http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_k